# Nuxt Frontend Conventions

Nuxt 4 (Vue 3) with the `app/` source root, Nitro server and SSR on (never `ssr: false` for a whole app). Follows `CLAUDE-FRONTEND.md` and `CLAUDE-FRONTEND-VUE.md` for everything not covered here. Pin `compatibilityDate` in `nuxt.config.ts` and bump it in its own commit.

## Layout

- `app/`: `app.vue` (`<NuxtLayout><NuxtPage /></NuxtLayout>`), `error.vue`, `pages/`, `layouts/`, `middleware/` (named route middleware), `plugins/`, `assets/css/main.scss` (custom properties, resets), plus the shared vocabulary (`components/`, `features/`, `composables/`, `api/`, `clients/`, `services/`, `config/`, `types/`...). `stores/` only if the project adopts Pinia.
- `server/`: `api/` (Nitro routes), `middleware/`, `plugins/`. Server code never imports from `app/`.
- `shared/`: types in `shared/types/`; pure functions both sides must apply identically in `shared/services/` (imported via `#shared`), e.g. `resolveClientAddress`. Never keep two copies of a security rule.
- Pages stay thin: compose from `features/` and `components/`. No `app/utils/` or `server/utils/`; use `services/` and `clients/`.
- File names: pages `kebab-case.vue`, `index.vue`, `[tripId].vue`; layouts, middleware and plugins `camelCase` (`.client`/`.server` suffix when side-specific); Nitro routes `name.<method>.ts` (`health.get.ts`).

## Layouts and auth gating

- Route groups become named layouts: `default.vue` (public), `auth.vue` (login, register), `protected.vue` (signed in). A page opts in with `definePageMeta({ layout: 'protected', middleware: 'require-session' })`; a middleware name is its file name in kebab-case.
- Gate protected routes in three parts. `server/middleware/sessionCookieGate.ts` redirects a full-page request for a protected prefix with no session cookie to `/login` (presence check only, skips `/api/**` and assets). `app/middleware/requireSession.ts` reads the session query and returns `navigateTo('/login')` on 401. `layouts/protected.vue` renders only after the session query resolves; logout removes that query from the cache.
- The session cookie is `httpOnly`; client code never reads `document.cookie`.

## API client and proxies

- `api/apiClient.ts` exports `createApiClient()`; a `useApiClient()` composable memoizes one per request on `useNuxtApp()`. Never a module-level client (it would reuse the first user's cookie).
- Always send `X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest`. Browser base URL is `/api`; on the server it is `runtimeConfig.apiBaseUrl`. Server-side calls forward `cookie`, `x-request-id` and a single `X-Forwarded-For` from `resolveClientAddress(forwardedFor, socketAddress)` (the edge-appended last entry), so the backend rate-limits the user.
- The browser calls only its own origin. `server/api/[...path].ts` proxies `/api/<rest>` to the backend with `proxyRequest`, appending the query string (`getRequestURL(event).search`) and rewriting `X-Forwarded-For` through `resolveClientAddress` first. `server/api/ingest/[...path].ts` proxies PostHog to `runtimeConfig.posthogHost`. `server/api/health.get.ts` answers the container healthcheck without calling the backend. No `routeRules` proxy.

## Head, config, theme

- `useSeoMeta({ title, description, ogTitle })` per page; `app.head` for site-wide defaults; `useHead` only for tags `useSeoMeta` lacks. Fonts through `@nuxt/fonts` as CSS custom properties.
- Import group 1 is `vue`, `vue-router`, `#imports`, `#app`.
- `runtimeConfig` declares every variable with an empty default; values come from `NUXT_*` (server-only) and `NUXT_PUBLIC_*` at run time. Read via `useRuntimeConfig()`, never `process.env` or `import.meta.env`. The backend URL is server-only (`NUXT_API_BASE_URL`).
- Theme (`light`, `dark`, `system`) lives in a `useThemePreference` composable on `useState`, persisted to `localStorage` by `plugins/theme.client.ts`, applied as `data-theme` on `<html>`. An inline `useHead` script sets it before first paint to avoid a flash.
- Sentry via `@sentry/nuxt` (`sentry.client.config.ts`, `sentry.server.config.ts`, DSN from `NUXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN`); tag the backend's request ID. Upload source maps in CI only.

## Container

- Nitro `node-server` preset. Multi-stage on `node:22-alpine`, copy only `.output/` into the runtime stage, `USER node`, `HEALTHCHECK` on `/api/health`, `CMD ["node", ".output/server/index.mjs"]`.
- `.dockerignore` excludes `.git`, `node_modules`, `.nuxt`, `.output`, `.env*` and tests. All `NUXT_PUBLIC_*` values are read at run time, so no environment-specific build arguments.
